{"type":"text","timestamp":1794049000712,"sessionID":"ses_e4a6faf75ffeWknnGBCeXJ18Fc","part":{"id":"prt_1b5a6e3a70013Ai9mTjPMRh51C","messageID":"msg_1b5a4de15001ArSCTK6lWDvrUo","sessionID":"ses_e4a6faf75ffeWknnGBCeXJ18Fc","type":"text","text":"\n\n## Objective\n- Fix the reviewer-identified `TokenBucket` over-acquisition bug at the root cause, add regression tests, verify with `python3 -m pytest -q`, and commit to the current branch without pushing or switching branches.\n\n## Important Details\n- Working directory: `/home/user/latte-crew/var/worktrees/1107-41e94c`.\n- Branch: `crew/1107-41e94c`.\n- Current committed state before the review fix: `e61d921 Add thread-safe token bucket limiter`; tree expected clean because no post-review file edits have been written yet.\n- Original buggy implementation still in `ledgerkit/limiter.py`:\n  - `self._tolerance = _EPS * capacity`\n  - affordability check uses `self._tokens + self._tolerance >= n`\n  - reviewer cited lines `ledgerkit/limiter.py:24, 42, 52`\n- Reviewer bug:\n  - tolerance scales with capacity, so large capacities permit accepting requests for tokens that do not exist.\n  - repro: `rate=1, capacity=10**6`, fixed clock, `try_acquire(10**6)` empties bucket, then `try_acquire(1)` incorrectly succeeds again and `wait_time(1)` returns `0.0`.\n  - repro: `capacity=10**7`, after drain, 100 `try_acquire(1)` calls all succeed with no time passing.\n- Required fix direction:\n  - remove capacity-scaled tolerance.\n  - reviewer accepted either exact arithmetic (`fractions.Fraction` or integer ticks) or a tiny rounding-scale epsilon such as `1e-9 * max(1.0, n)` / `4 * sys.float_info.epsilon * max(n, tokens)`.\n  - `wait_time` must return a value that, when added to the current clock, makes `try_acquire(n)` succeed.\n- Required regression tests:\n  - large capacity such as `10**6` or `10**7`: after draining, `try_acquire(1)` must be `False` and `wait_time(1)` must be about `1 / rate`.\n  - existing/expanded cycle test with rates `0.1`, `3.0`, `7.0`, capacities `1`, `5`, `100`, `1000`, thousands of cycles, must pass.\n  - concurrency test on a large-capacity bucket with a fixed clock asserting total acquired is at most `capacity`.\n- API/validation constraints remain:\n  - `TokenBucket(rate, capacity, clock=time.monotonic)`.\n  - starts full.\n  - `try_acquire(n=1)` returns `True` and consumes only when enough tokens exist; otherwise returns `False` and consumes nothing.\n  - `wait_time(n=1)` returns `0.0` if already available and consumes nothing.\n  - `ValueError` for `rate <= 0`, `capacity <= 0`, `n <= 0`, or `n > capacity`.\n  - lazy refill capped at `capacity`; backward clock resets internal time without adding tokens.\n- Scratch prototype status:\n  - tested an exact `fractions.Fraction` implementation via a temporary `python3 - <<'EOF'` command, not by editing repo files.\n  - prototype fixed the large-capacity over-acquire repro.\n  - prototype passed `rate=0.1` cycle combinations.\n  - prototype failed with `AssertionError: (3.0, 1, 1)` in the cycle test.\n  - likely cause: `wait_time` searched by incrementing the delay `w` with `math.nextafter(w, inf)` instead of advancing the representable candidate clock value; for larger clock values, many small `w` increments do not move `time_value + w` to the next useful float.\n\n## Work State\n### Completed\n- Initial implementation of `/home/user/latte-crew/var/worktrees/1107-41e94c/ledgerkit/limiter.py` and `/home/user/latte-crew/var/worktrees/1107-41e94c/tests/test_limiter.py`.\n- Fixed initial test arithmetic failures and got `python3 -m pytest -q` to pass with `23 passed`.\n- Committed that initial work as `e61d921` on `crew/1107-41e94c`.\n- Analyzed reviewer feedback and confirmed the bug is the capacity-scaled tolerance.\n- Prototyped an exact `Fraction`-based `TokenBucket` in scratch and confirmed it fixes the reported large-capacity repro.\n\n### Active\n- Need to replace the committed float/tolerance implementation in `ledgerkit/limiter.py` with a root-cause fix.\n- Need to make `wait_time` robust by searching the next representable future clock value, not merely incrementing the returned delay.\n- Need to add the reviewer-requested regression tests to `tests/test_limiter.py`.\n- Need to rerun the full pytest suite and commit the fix.\n\n### Blocked\n- none\n\n## Next Move\n1. Rewrite `/home/user/latte-crew/var/worktrees/1107-41e94c/ledgerkit/limiter.py` using exact `fractions.Fraction` state for `rate`, `capacity`, `tokens`, and internal time, with no capacity-scaled tolerance; validate finite positive inputs to avoid `Fraction(float('inf'))`/NaN issues.\n2. Implement `wait_time(n)` by:\n   - refilling with `Fraction(clock())`;\n   - returning `0.0` if tokens are already sufficient;\n   - computing exact `delta = (n - tokens) / rate`;\n   - starting from `candidate = self._time_value + float(delta)`;\n   - if `candidate <= self._time_value`, set `candidate = math.nextafter(self._time_value, math.inf)`;\n   - if exact token gain at `candidate` is insufficient, set `candidate = math.nextafter(candidate, math.inf)`;\n   - returning a delay that reproduces `candidate` when added to `self._time_value`, normally `candidate - self._time_value`.\n3. Add tests to `/home/user/latte-crew/var/worktrees/1107-41e94c/tests/test_limiter.py` for:\n   - `rate=1, capacity=10**6` and `10**7`: drain, assert `try_acquire(1)` is `False`, `wait_time(1)` approx `1.0`;\n   - large-capacity fixed-clock concurrency where total acquired is at most `capacity`;\n   - keep/verify the multi-rate/capacity cycle test.\n4. Run `python3 -m pytest -q` from `/home/user/latte-crew/var/worktrees/1107-41e94c`, confirm the actual result, then commit the fix to `crew/1107-41e94c` without pushing or switching branches.\n\n## Relevant Files\n- `/home/user/latte-crew/var/worktrees/1107-41e94c/ledgerkit/limiter.py`: current buggy `TokenBucket`; target file for the root-cause fix.\n- `/home/user/latte-crew/var/worktrees/1107-41e94c/tests/test_limiter.py`: existing tests plus location for the required regression tests.\n- `/home/user/latte-crew/var/worktrees/1107-41e94c/README.md`: documents running tests with `python3 -m pytest -q`.\n- `/home/user/latte-crew/var/worktrees/1107-41e94c/tests/test_money.py`: style reference for direct-import pytest tests.","time":{"start":1794048975784,"end":1794049000707}}}
