{"type":"text","timestamp":1794049214654,"sessionID":"ses_e4a6faf75ffeWknnGBCeXJ18Fc","part":{"id":"prt_1b5aa3c63001SYb1HnPvW4VfgL","messageID":"msg_1b5aa0a530011DnqrNrPPt6EPa","sessionID":"ses_e4a6faf75ffeWknnGBCeXJ18Fc","type":"text","text":"\n\n## Objective\n- Fix the reviewer-identified `TokenBucket` over-acquisition bug at the root cause, add regression tests, verify with `python3 -m pytest -q`, and commit to the current branch without pushing or switching branches.\n\n## Important Details\n- Working directory: `/home/user/latte-crew/var/worktrees/1107-41e94c`.\n- Branch: `crew/1107-41e94c`.\n- Last commit before the active fix: `e61d921 Add thread-safe token bucket limiter`.\n- The reviewer bug was caused by capacity-scaled tolerance:\n  - old line: `self._tolerance = _EPS * capacity`\n  - old affordability check: `self._tokens + self._tolerance >= n`\n  - large capacities allowed acquiring tokens that did not exist, e.g. `rate=1, capacity=10**6`, drain, then `try_acquire(1)` wrongly succeeded and `wait_time(1)` returned `0.0`.\n- Chosen root-cause fix: exact `fractions.Fraction` arithmetic for `rate`, `capacity`, `tokens`, and internal time; no capacity-scaled tolerance.\n- Current uncommitted rewrite in `/home/user/latte-crew/var/worktrees/1107-41e94c/ledgerkit/limiter.py`:\n  - imports `math`, `threading`, `time`, `fractions.Fraction`.\n  - validates `rate`, `capacity`, `n`, and clock values are finite and positive where required.\n  - stores `_rate`, `_capacity`, `_tokens`, and `_time` as `Fraction`; keeps `_time_value` as the float clock value.\n  - `try_acquire(n)` succeeds only when `_tokens >= n`, then subtracts exactly.\n  - `wait_time(n)` returns `0.0` if already affordable; otherwise computes exact `required = self._time + (n - self._tokens) / self._rate` and searches representable float clock candidates so that advancing by the returned delay makes the bucket affordable.\n- Required regression tests still to add:\n  - large capacity such as `10**6` or `10**7`: after draining, `try_acquire(1)` must be `False` and `wait_time(1)` must be about `1 / rate`.\n  - fixed-clock concurrency on a large-capacity bucket asserting total acquired is at most `capacity`.\n  - preserve/verify multi-rate/capacity cycle behavior, e.g. rates `0.1`, `3.0`, `7.0` and capacities `1`, `5`, `100`, `1000`.\n- API constraints:\n  - `TokenBucket(rate, capacity, clock=time.monotonic)`.\n  - starts full.\n  - `try_acquire(n=1)` consumes only when enough tokens exist.\n  - `wait_time(n=1)` returns `0.0` if already available and consumes nothing.\n  - `ValueError` for invalid `rate`, `capacity`, or `n`.\n  - lazy refill capped at `capacity`; backward clock resets internal time without adding tokens.\n- `wait_time` robustness detail:\n  - the previous prototype failure for `(3.0, 1, 1)` was due to incrementing the returned delay instead of advancing the candidate clock value.\n  - the current implementation advances `target` with `math.nextafter(target, math.inf)` and validates the final delay by checking `self._time_value + delay` against the exact `required` time.\n\n## Work State\n### Completed\n- Initial implementation and tests were committed as `e61d921` on `crew/1107-41e94c`.\n- Confirmed the reviewer bug and reproduced the large-capacity over-acquire behavior.\n- Prototyped an exact `Fraction`-based implementation in scratch and confirmed it fixes the reported large-capacity repro.\n- Rewrote `/home/user/latte-crew/var/worktrees/1107-41e94c/ledgerkit/limiter.py` with the exact `Fraction` implementation and candidate-clock `wait_time` logic.\n- Inspected current `tests/test_limiter.py` and confirmed existing tests are present, but reviewer-requested regression tests are not yet added.\n\n### Active\n- Need to verify the uncommitted `ledgerkit/limiter.py` rewrite against the existing test suite.\n- Need to add the reviewer-requested regression tests to `/home/user/latte-crew/var/worktrees/1107-41e94c/tests/test_limiter.py`.\n- Need to confirm large-capacity, concurrency, and cycle tests pass.\n- Need to commit the fix to `crew/1107-41e94c` without pushing or switching branches.\n\n### Blocked\n- none\n\n## Next Move\n1. Run `python3 -m pytest -q` from `/home/user/latte-crew/var/worktrees/1107-41e94c` to verify the new exact `Fraction` implementation passes the existing tests.\n2. Add regression tests to `/home/user/latte-crew/var/worktrees/1107-41e94c/tests/test_limiter.py` for large-capacity drain behavior, fixed-clock concurrency, and the required cycle combinations.\n3. Rerun `python3 -m pytest -q`, confirm all tests pass, then commit the fix to `crew/1107-41e94c`.\n\n## Relevant Files\n- `/home/user/latte-crew/var/worktrees/1107-41e94c/ledgerkit/limiter.py`: contains the uncommitted root-cause `Fraction` rewrite of `TokenBucket`.\n- `/home/user/latte-crew/var/worktrees/1107-41e94c/tests/test_limiter.py`: existing test suite; needs the required regression tests added.\n- `/home/user/latte-crew/var/worktrees/1107-41e94c/README.md`: documents running tests with `python3 -m pytest -q`.\n- `/home/user/latte-crew/var/worktrees/1107-41e94c/tests/test_money.py`: style reference for direct-import pytest tests.","time":{"start":1794049195107,"end":1794049214649}}}
